   "notes": "Below these concentrations a substance is not radioactive material or radioactive waste, which is the UK equivalent of clearance. The catch-all of 0.01 Bq/g applies to any artificial radionuclide the table does not list, so unlisted nuclides are limited rather than unregulated. Part 2 paragraph 7 places a substance outside the regulation when none of its radionuclides has a half-life exceeding 100 seconds, which is a test on the whole material. These values are a separate derivation from the exemption values of EU directive 2013/59/Euratom Annex VII, based on a 10 microsievert per year dose criterion via Euratom RP 122 part 1, and are generally ten times stricter, so they are not expected to match EU_BSS_clearance or UK_IRR17_notification."
